  "description": "Turns Hlibz.Results into HTTP responses with one error body everywhere: result.ToHttpResult() for minimal APIs (or a plain Result returned from a handler with WithResultResponses()) and result.ToActionResult() for controllers map Success/Error/Invalid/NotFound/Unauthorized/Forbidden/Conflict/Unavailable to 200/400/400/404/401/403/409/503 (remappable, e.g. 422 for validation), with { message, code, validation_errors } on every failure, the authorization gate's own 401/403 included. Optional Crunch-style envelope ({ data, is_success, status, message, code, validation_errors }), WithResultEnvelopes() for handlers returning a plain Result, validation keys cased by your JSON naming policy per path segment, and an error code catalog endpoint listing every code your API returns.",
